From 1d3a3a7bfec94b0c50d88bbbfb9254898835c025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:19:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): vectorize post-load weight prep, add artifact
 cache, and warm first-prefill state

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488.

Rationale:
1. Post-load MoE scale-code and FP4 weight preparation across 58 layers previously ran separate min/max/any reductions in _row_deltas, computed 4-bit nibbles and overlay_byte_codes copies even when all experts were narrow, permuted 64-byte FP4 TMA slabs byte-by-byte instead of as 8-byte int64 words, and invoked torch.cuda.empty_cache() after every submodule in process_weights_after_loading whenever reserved memory exceeded 80% of total memory even when the submodule allocated no new segments.
2. In-place 12-bit BF16 packing (pack_bf16_weight(in_place=True)) previously staged and copied every 1,024-row chunk across all 43,264 lm_head rows even though output bytes [1.5*K*start, 1.5*K*end) lie strictly below unread input bytes [2*K*start, 2*K*out_features) once start >= 3,072 and 3*end <= 4*start. Similarly, TP3 rank 2 _trim_padded_groups unpacked 12,288 wq_b rows and repacked 8,192 rows across 59 layers even when tilelang_weight was already packed in contiguous 128x128 tiles.
3. Subsequent starts recomputed all pack12 and MoE scale-code artifacts from scratch; API server model resolution eagerly imported vllm.models.deepseek_v4_1.nvidia.model (pulling in tilelang and flashinfer before worker spawn); get_tokenizer reloaded AutoConfig even when model_config.hf_config was already loaded; and the first eager prefill request after startup lazily constructed 59 layers of L2 prefetch device pointer tables (_build_l2_prefetch) and the SP prefill side stream (sp_prefill._side_stream).

Changes:
- Vectorize _row_deltas (single-pass torch.aminmax on positive scales), SWAR _pack_crumbs / _pack_nibbles, fused encode_expert_scale_codes, and 8-byte int64 tile_expert_weights / pack_weight_tiles / unpack_weight_tiles.
- Stage only the first 3,072 overlapping rows in pack_bf16_weight(in_place=True) and pack remaining rows directly in place in non-overlapping geometric steps (end = min(out_features, (4 * start) // 3)).
- Slice wq_b.tilelang_weight[:q_rows * (k_q // TILE_WEIGHT_K)] directly in _trim_padded_groups when tilelang_weight_packed is True.
- Guard release_device_memory_under_pressure on torch.cuda.memory_reserved(target_device) > reserved_before.
- Add an optional per-rank on-disk post-load artifact cache (vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/tilelang/postload_cache.py) with single-thread background atomic staging writes (*.tmp.<pid> -> os.replace, >=8 GiB free disk guard, dead-PID staging cleanup, loading_done() barrier) and cached direct reads with 4-slice (first, first+1, last, per-boot random) byte-for-byte spot verification before in-place mutation.
- Make vllm/models/deepseek_v41/__init__.py and vl_model.py lazy, pass config=model_config.hf_config into get_tokenizer for TokenizersBackend subclasses, and warm _build_l2_prefetch() and sp_prefill._side_stream() during DeepseekV4Model.declare_kernels().

Quality:
100% bit-identical (torch.equal) packed BF16 weights, exception tables, MoE tiled weights, UE8M0 scale codes, trimmed wq_b weights, and model outputs.

Tests:
- pytest tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_postload_startup.py tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_expert_scale_codes.py tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41.py tests/v1/attention/test_sparse_indexer_decode_seq_lens.py (170 passed across 2 boots).

Upstream status: local startup and post-load optimization for DeepSeek-V4.1 on GB10.
